# Vue Router history-mode fallback for Render Static Sites. Render supports
# this file the same way Netlify does (checked from the publish directory).
# This makes the rewrite rule version-controlled instead of a manual
# dashboard setting that's easy to forget when recreating the service.
#
# IMPORTANT: this must NOT catch requests for files that actually exist
# under /assets/ - Render (like Netlify) only falls through to this rule
# when no real file matches the request path first, so a request for an
# asset that genuinely exists on disk is served directly and never reaches
# this rule. Only truly missing files (including stale-hash 404s) or
# client-side routes (e.g. /products/abc) fall through to index.html.
/*    /index.html   200
